      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "sound",
      "title": "Finding the words in a line with no spaces",
      "text": "Read ผมอ่านหนังสือครับ from the end. ครับ closes a polite sentence, so it is a word of its own. A vowel written in front of a consonant (เ แ โ ไ ใ) starts a syllable, so the break comes just before it: ผม | อ่าน | หนังสือ | ครับ. Words you already know are the best guide: look for them first, and the rest is usually one new word.",
      "explains": [
        "th.script.no-spaces",
        "th.practice.vowels-before"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
